FAQ = [
 ("Do 2015–2020 F-150 floor liners fit a 2021–2026 F-150?",
  "Often, yes, which surprises people. Husky lists its WeatherBeater 94041 set for 2015–2026 SuperCrew trucks, and LASFIT, Weize and Mixsuper list 2015–2025 or 2015–2026 SuperCrew coverage on the listings on this page. The cab floor pan carried over into the 14th generation. What did not carry over is every rear-floor option: trucks with the fold-flat rear storage need a different second-row piece. Match the rear floor first, then the year range."),
 ("How do I know if my F-150 has fold-flat rear storage?",
  "Lift the rear seat cushions. If a hinged, flat load floor unfolds out of the space under the seat and locks level with the cushion base, you have the fold-flat storage option. If you see open plastic bins or a lockable box under the cushion and no folding floor, you do not. The window sticker also lists it. The difference matters because a full-width second-row liner cut for a plain floor will not sit flat around the fold-flat hardware."),
 ("Which liners fit the F-150 Lightning?",
  "The Lightning uses the SuperCrew cab, so most SuperCrew liners list it. On this page, LASFIT names 2022–2025 Lightning, Mixsuper names Lightning, and Husky's 94041 title lists 2022–2026 Lightning. Some budget listings stop at gas trucks, so rely on a listing that names Lightning rather than assuming. The frunk is a separate liner; none of these sets include it."),
 ("Are WeatherBeater liners better than cheaper TPE liners?",
  "They are better documented, not magic. Husky says WeatherBeater liners are laser-measured with vehicle-specific data, made in the USA from its ProGard material, use StayPut nibs on the underside, and carry a lifetime warranty against cracks and breaks. Budget TPE sets are also laser-cut to a vehicle and often fit well, but their makers publish fewer specs and warranty terms are shorter. You pay roughly $40–$80 more for the paper trail."),
 ("Will liners fit an F-150 XL with a vinyl floor?",
  "Usually, but check the title. Husky's 94041 listing says 'with carpet', and some makers cut the underside nibs for carpet grip. On a vinyl floor a nibbed liner still sits in place because the walls lock it into the footwell, but it can shift more under the pedals. Use the factory retention posts where the listing supports them, and keep the driver liner anchored before the first drive."),
 ("Do I need front-row liners that match a bench seat or buckets?",
  "The F-150 comes with a 40/20/40 front bench or two buckets with a center console. Most front-row liners on this page are two-piece driver and passenger mats that fit either layout because the center floor is covered by the console or the bench's center section. The bench layout leaves a strip of carpet in the middle exposed; if you carry a middle passenger, look for a center hump piece."),
 ("Can I put a liner on top of the factory carpet mat?",
  "No. Remove the factory mat first. A liner stacked on a carpet mat can slide forward and catch the accelerator or brake pedal, which is the failure every maker warns about. The liner is designed to sit on the carpet itself and hook to the factory retention posts on the driver side."),
 ("How do I clean TPE or WeatherBeater liners without making them slippery?",
  "Pull them out, hose them down, and scrub with mild soap and a stiff brush. Skip tire shine and silicone protectants, which make the surface slick under wet boots. Let them dry fully before reinstalling so water doesn't sit under the liner on the carpet. In winter, a quick shake-out every few days prevents salt slush from spilling over the walls."),
 ("Do these sets cover the whole rear floor under the seat?",
  "The second-row pieces on this page are one-piece liners that run across the rear floor, including the center hump. Coverage under the seat depends on the rear storage type. On fold-flat trucks the under-seat area is part of the storage mechanism, so liners stop at the hardware. Read the listing photos for how far back the rear liner reaches."),
 ("How long do floor liners last on a work truck?",
  "Several years for most TPE and WeatherBeater liners. Husky's lifetime warranty covers cracks and breaks, which is the common failure on cheaper rigid liners in cold climates. LASFIT rates its TPE for −13°F to 167°F. Heel wear on the driver side is the first thing to show; a liner with a textured heel pad area lasts longer for drivers who wear work boots."),
]

